{
  "description": "Forward-MINOR routing along a declared `extends` chain (SPEC §5.2 \"Declared extension\", §7.2 item 3) as every runtime applies it. A consumer implements `implements.typeUri`, whose payload schema is `implements.payloadSchema` (JSON text, as a generated module carries it). `extends` is the declarations in force — bare request Type URI to the MAJOR.MINOR it directly extends — handed to the runtime's own lookup. Each case reads `document` (JSON text) for the implemented version and must reach `verdict`: `accept`, or the code it is refused with — `unsupportedVersion` for the same specification and variant at a version the chain does not reach, `unsupportedType` for anything else (another slug, the same slug under another authority, another variant). For an accepted case the payload read must equal `payload` (a document read forward is pruned to the members the implemented schema knows), `extended` says whether it was read forward, and a response to it is typed `answerType`: the RECEIVED type's `#response`, never the implemented version's.",
  "implements": {
    "typeUri": "https://example.com/spec/vector/grant/0.1",
    "payloadSchema": "{\"$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"subject\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"role\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"subject\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}"
  },
  "extends": {
    "https://example.com/spec/vector/grant/0.2": "0.1",
    "https://example.com/spec/vector/grant/0.3": "0.2",
    "https://example.com/spec/vector/grant/0.6": "0.5",
    "https://other.example/spec/vector/grant/0.2": "0.1"
  },
